   "headers": [
    "2",
    "2.1 Contractor will provide & utilize a Work Order Management System (WOMS)\nA. Contractor will utilize the WOMS to, at minimum:\ni. Document information for meter and transmitter exchanges:\n1. Date and time of installation\n2. Address of the installation\n3. Name of person who performed the work\n4. Old meter info (meter ID, Size, etc.)\n5. Final register reading for the old meter (confirm the\nregister read is greater than the last billing read in CIS. If\nnot, report to COB Staff).\n6. New meter info (meter ID, Size)- Validate new meter ID\nagainst inventory.\n7. New meter register read at install\n8. Old smartpoint serial #\n9. New smartpoint serial #\n10. Photographs of the work\na. Site before & after installation of meter & smartpoint,\nb. The old meter with the screen and meter ID visible &\nthe new meter with the screen and meter ID visible\n(single photo)\nc. The old & new smartpoints in the same photo\nB. COB personnel shall have access to the WOMS to review as needed.\nC. Contractor will utilize captured meter data within the WOMS to provide a\nproperly formatted digital file for upload into the City\u2019s CIS (Cayenta) that\nincludes, at minimum:\ni. Address for the exchange\nii. Date meter was exchanged\niii. Meter ID for the old meter\niv. A register read for the old meter at time of exchange\nv. Meter ID for the new meter\nvi. A register read for the new meter at time of exchange\nvii. The new Smartpoint ID\nD. Contractor will utilize WOMS to manage product inventory within Contractor\u2019s\npossession throughout the project."
   ],
